From eb427630897e472e470f2830371a090f0a79eb08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:42:50 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 15/26] ipa: simple: Contrast autofocus

Add an Af algorithm to the simple IPA, on the focus measure of the
software ISP statistics (afSharpness / afSum over the central third).

The lens position is normalised, 0.0 at the far end and 1.0 at the near
end. A scan steps the lens over the range (coarse), then around the best
position (fine), and stops at the sharpest one; a scan whose contrast is
too low fails and parks the lens at a default position. AfModeContinuous
(the default) scans at start and again when the measure drops for a few
consecutive statistics; AfModeAuto scans on AfTriggerStart; AfModeManual
leaves the lens to LensPosition. AfState is reported in the metadata.

The IPA requests lens moves through a new setLensPosition event, which
the software ISP forwards. The simple pipeline handler maps the
normalised position to its LensPosition range (the lens map of the
configuration file) and moves the lens unless the camera is in
AfModeManual; LensPosition requests apply only in AfModeManual.

The algorithm is enabled per sensor by an Af entry in the tuning file,
for sensors with a focus lens.

Signed-off-by: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
